<article class="env-corollary" id="0238">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0238">Corollary <span data-tag="0238">4.5.7.23</span>.</a> Suppose we are given an inverse system of $\infty $-categories </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \cdots \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(3) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(2) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(1) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(0) \]
</div>
<p> where each of the transition functors $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n-1)$ is an isofibration. Then the limit $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}= \varprojlim _{n} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n)$ is an $\infty $-category, whose core $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\simeq }$ is the inverse limit $\varprojlim _{n} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n)^{\simeq }$. In other words, a morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an isomorphism if and only if its image in each $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}(n)$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Example <a data-tag="034E" href="/tag/034E">4.5.7.8</a>, Corollary <a data-tag="034L" href="/tag/034L">4.5.7.13</a>, and Corollary <a data-tag="034U" href="/tag/034U">4.5.7.22</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
